## ✅ **Core Pod-Level Alerts (Must-Have)**

| # | Alert Name                          | Purpose                                                                 |
| - | ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1 | **Pod Not Running**                 | Detects pods in states other than `Running` (e.g., `Pending`, `Failed`) |
| 2 | **Pod Restart Detected**            | Captures any restarts in the last N minutes                             |
| 3 | **CrashLoopBackOff**                | Detects if containers are stuck in restart loops                        |
| 4 | **Pod Uptime Too Low**              | Alerts if a pod was recently restarted or created                       |
| 5 | **Pod Uptime Too High**             | Detects long-living pods that haven’t been rolled (e.g., > 7 days)      |
| 6 | **Pod CPU Usage Too High**          | Catches pods consuming unexpected CPU                                   |
| 7 | **Pod Memory Usage Too High**       | Catches memory-hungry pods that may OOM                                 |
| 8 | **Pod Not Ready**                   | Flags pods whose containers fail readiness probes                       |
| 9 | **Unscheduled Pods (Pending Long)** | Detects pods stuck in `Pending` due to scheduling/resource issues       |

---

## 📌 Bonus / Optional Alerts (Advanced Monitoring)

| #  | Alert Name                       | When to use                                                              |
| -- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 10 | **Pod Evicted**                  | Detects pods removed from nodes due to resource pressure                 |
| 11 | **Pod Distribution Imbalance**   | Too many replicas of a service running on same node                      |
| 12 | **OOMKilled Detection**          | Use `container_status_terminated_reason` with `reason="OOMKilled"`       |
| 13 | **Container Image Pull Error**   | Detects `ImagePullBackOff`, etc. using `container_status_waiting_reason` |
| 14 | **Node-to-Pod Saturation Ratio** | Helps with planning scale-up / bin-packing checks                        |

